----

Migrations (server): Run a single migration with server/run-migration.js. Path is relative to the server directory. From repo root:
  node server/run-migration.js migrations/<filename>.sql
Example:
  node server/run-migration.js migrations/037_get_player_stats_enhanced_single_row.sql
Loads .env from the server directory; uses DATABASE_URL. Run migrations in order by number when applying multiple.

----

Git (default): When the user asks to stage, commit, or push without naming a branch, use **`main`** on **`origin`**: `git checkout main`, `git pull origin main` as needed, then `git push origin main`. Do not push to a `cursor/*` or other feature branch unless they explicitly name it. (See also `.cursor/rules/git-origin-main.mdc`.)

